### HTTP examples (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
@base = http://localhost:8080

### Entrega 1 — eco
GET {{base}}/books
###
GET {{base}}/books/42
###
POST {{base}}/books
###
PUT {{base}}/books/42
###
DELETE {{base}}/books/42

### Desde entrega 2 (200) / entrega 3 (201 + Location)
POST {{base}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn":"978-1","title":"DDD","author":"Evans","year":2003}

### Usar el id/Location devuelto, no suponer un libro precargado
GET {{base}}/books/1

### Listado JSON (entrega 2)
GET {{base}}/books
Accept: application/json

### Modificación JSON (entrega 2; sustituir el 1 por el id devuelto)
PUT {{base}}/books/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn":"978-1","title":"DDD 2.ª ed.","author":"Evans","year":2004}

### Borrado (entrega 2; sustituir el 1 por el id devuelto)
DELETE {{base}}/books/1

### Desde entrega 6: validación 400 con payload
POST {{base}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn":"978-1","title":" ","author":"Evans","year":2003}
